s (especially Ohio) and in temperate South America. The Herbarium supports research and teaching at OSU and receives frequent use by researchers from other academic institutions, as well as by staff from governmental agencies such as the Ohio Department of Natural Resources.","logo":"https://sernecportal.org/portal/content/collicon/os.jpg","url":"http://herbarium.osu.edu/","emllink":"https://sernecportal.org/portal/collections/datasets/emlhandler.php?collid=239","archivelink":"https://midwestherbaria.org/portal/content/dwca/os_dwc-a.zip","contacts":[{"email":"hbrown@mailbox.sc.edu"},{"email":"hbrown@mailbox.sc.edu"},{"email":"freudenstein.1@osu.edu"},{"last_name":"John V. Freudenstein, Director","email":"freudenstein.1@osu.edu"},{"first_name":"Jeff","last_name":"Rose","role":"Curator","email":"rose.873@osu.edu"},{"last_name":"John V. Freudenstein, Director","email":"freudenstein.1@osu.edu"},{"first_name":"Jeff","last_name":"Rose","role":"Curator","email":"rose.873@osu.edu"}],"data_rights":"CC4 BY-NC","publisher":"5946eff1-b27a-4651-8323-2ab8d62ef328","totalCount":37090,"hitRatio":0.000026961445133459154},{"uuid":"471835cc-feb6-4d05-a8d1-62ce71399326","itemCount":1,"name":"Virginia Polytechnic Institute and State University, Massey Herbarium","description":"The Massey Herbarium (VPI) at Virginia Tech is an active and growing collection that seeks to represent the floristic diversity of the central Appalachian and Mid-Atlantic regions. Growing from a small teaching collection, the herbarium was established as a state repository in 1927. As of 2022, accessioned vascular plant specimens numbered 111,000. It is estimated that about 65% are from Virginia, the balance from all parts of North American. Groups particularly well represented are ferns (especially Isoetes), Poaceae, Cyperaceae (especially Carex), and Asteraceae (Eupatorium, Packera, Solidago).","logo":"https://sernecportal.org/portal/content/collicon/vpi.jpg","url":"http://masseyherbarium.org/","emllink":"https://sernecportal.org/portal/collections/datasets/emlhandler.php?collid=271","archivelink":"https://sernecportal.org/portal/content/dwca/vpi_dwc-a.zip","contacts":[{"email":"hbrown@mailbox.sc.edu"},{"email":"hbrown@mailbox.sc.edu"},{"email":"metzgar@vt.edu"},{"last_name":"Jordan Metzgar","email":"metzgar@vt.edu"},{"last_name":"Jordan Metzgar","email":"metzgar@vt.edu"}],"data_rights":"CC3 BY-NC","publisher":"42f2a0a4-5981-4874-88d5-9efb1e8d52c9","totalCount":61826,"hitRatio":0.000016174424999191277},{"uuid":"6258d160-a7aa-4937-bce3-3538eebd374f","itemCount":1,"name":"Duke University Vascular Plant Collection","description":"Duke Herbarium houses more than 425,000 specimens of vascular plants, including 821 types. The collection is especially rich in accessions from the Southeastern United States, in particular for the Carolinas, and Mesoamerica. The vascular plant herbarium contains an important collection of over 22,000 sheets from La Selva&nbsp;in Costa Rica.","logo":"https://sernecportal.org/portal/content/collicon/duke.png","url":null,"emllink":"https://sernecportal.org/portal/collections/datasets/emlhandler.php?collid=192","archivelink":"https://sernecportal.org/portal/content/dwca/duke_dwc-a.zip","contacts":[{"email":"hbrown@mailbox.sc.edu"},{"email":"hbrown@mailbox.sc.edu"},{"email":"mdw26@duke.edu"},{"first_name":"Michael D.","last_name":"Windham","email":"mdw26@duke.edu"},{"first_name":"Michael D.","last_name":"Windham","email":"mdw26@duke.edu"}],"data_rights":"CC4 BY-NC","publisher":"42f2a0a4-5981-4874-88d5-9efb1e8d52c9","totalCount":157944,"hitRatio":0.000006331357949653042},{"uuid":"72d4c3c7-3413-4588-a803-e1a63e0d7c6c","itemCount":1,"name":"Vanderbilt University Herbarium","description":"","logo":"https://portal.torcherbaria.org/portal/content/collicon/vdb.jpg","url":"http://www.brit.org/departments/herbarium","emllink":"https://sernecportal.org/portal/collections/datasets/emlhandler.php?collid=264","archivelink":"https://sernecportal.org/portal/content/dwca/brit-vdb_dwc-a.zip","contacts":[{"email":"hbrown@mailbox.sc.edu"},{"email":"hbrown@mailbox.sc.edu"},{"email":"herbarium@brit.org"},{"first_name":"Tiana","last_name":"Rehman","role":"Herbarium Director","email":"herbarium@brit.org"},{"first_name":"Ashley","last_name":"Bales","role":"Collections Manager","email":"abales@fwbg.org"},{"first_name":"Tiana","last_name":"Rehman","role":"Herbarium Director","email":"herbarium@brit.org"},{"first_name":"Ashley","last_name":"Bales","role":"Collections Manager","email":"abales@fwbg.org"}],"data_rights":"CC0","publisher":"42f2a0a4-5981-4874-88d5-9efb1e8d52c9","totalCount":336975,"hitRatio":0.000002967579197269827},{"uuid":"a6eee223-cf3b-4079-8bb2-b77dad8cae9d","itemCount":1,"name":"NMNH Extant Specimen Records (USNM, US)","description":"Public records of accessioned specimens and observations curated by the National Museum of Natural History, Smithsonian Institution. These data are from the Departments of Botany, Entomology, Invertebrate Zoology and Vertebrate Zoology (Amphibians & Reptiles, Birds, Fishes, and Mammals) and include more than 270,000 primary type specimen records.","logo":"http://collections.nmnh.si.edu/ipt/logo.do?r=nmnh_extant_dwc-a","url":"http://collections.nmnh.si.edu","emllink":"https://collections.nmnh.si.edu/ipt/eml.do?r=nmnh_extant_dwc-a","archivelink":"https://collections.nmnh.si.edu/ipt/archive.do?r=nmnh_extant_dwc-a","contacts":[{"first_name":"Thomas","last_name":"Orrell","role":"Deputy Director, Research Informatics Program","email":"orrellt@si.edu"},{"last_name":"Informatics and Data Science Center - Digital Stewardship","role":"IPT Administrator","email":"informaticshelp@si.edu"},{"first_name":"Thomas","last_name":"Orrell","role":"Deputy Director, Research Informatics Program","email":"orrellt@si.edu"},{"last_name":"Informatics and Data Science Center - Digital Stewardship","role":"IPT Administrator","email":"informaticshelp@si.edu"},{"first_name":"Chris","last_name":"Tuccinardi","role":"Informati